The potatoes are now boiling in the pot.
It already smells lovely in the kitchen.
I take out a large frying pan.
I read the next instructions in the recipe.
The next part is important.
It says: "First melt a thick piece of butter in the pan."
I cut some butter and put it in the pan.
The butter quickly sizzles on the hot metal.
I read on: "Afterwards form the meat into round balls."
I use a spoon to form the meat.
It is a bit difficult, but they turn out nice and round.
I carefully place them in the hot pan.
The recipe continues: "Then fry them until they are crisp and brown."
I turn down the heat a little.
They need to fry for about fifteen minutes.
I turn them often so they do not burn.
They smell fantastic and get a good color.
Now the meatballs and the potatoes are almost ready.
I am looking forward to Kasper and Sara arriving.
It is absolutely perfect timing.
